<CENTER><div class="header"><B>AGN Employment Opportunities</B></div></CENTER>
<br>
<div class="default" align=center>
<strong>TCG Lead Editor</strong></div>
<br>
<div class="default_9" align=justify>
<strong>Description</strong><br>
Functions / Responsibilities:<br>
<ol>
<li>Organize and stay in constant contact with staff writers to provide a strict schedule that ensures publish dates are meet each day.</li>
<li>Give feedback and provide ideas to writers to help them get quality material ready to be published.</li>
<li>Create daily discussion threads that will appeal to the community as a whole.</li>
<li>Update the decks database section immediatly after tournament results become available from various sites on the internet.</li>
<li>Create internal and external images that are used to help promote the articles.</li>
<li>Editing and posting of daily updates and articles.</li>
</ol>
Secondary Functions:<br>
<ol>
<li>Ensure different sections of the sites are up to date and focused at the current formats.</li>
<li>Approach potential writers to be new additions to the staff.</li>
<li>Provide daily updates to an AGN Network Correspondent via email and phone of the current writer schedule and plans for each update.</li>
</ol>
<br>
<strong>Qualifications</strong><br>
Education and Training:<br>
Bachelor's Degree required. 4 years of related experience with 2 years of college would be an acceptable substitution.
<br><br>
Knowledge, Skills and Abilities:<br>
<ol>
<li>Significant experience playing Magic: the Gathering is required.</li>
<li>HTML, editorial critiquing, and graphics abilities are required.  Past experience is highly desired.</li>
<li>Individual must be self-motivated. Ability to fulfill project tasks with minimal supervision required.</li>
<li>Ability to provide constructive feedback to both the writers and AGN staff is  required.</li>
<li>Effective verbal communication skills required. Effective written communication skills highly desired.</li>
<li>Familiarity with the VS System card game and the gaming industry in general is desired.</li>
</ol>
Other Requirements:
<ol>
<li>Individual must be located in the United States.</li>
<li>Typical hours are 9am-3pm and 10pm-12am EST, Sunday-Thursday. But individual must be able to work whenever necessary to ensure that the next day's update is 100% ready and on time.</li>
<li>Applicant must have a Cell Phone and main computer with at least a Pentium III and 256 ram. A laptop as well is highly desired.</li>
<li>Occasional weekend travel to large events is a possibility once job familiarity is established.</li>

</ol>
The above is intended to describe the general content of and the requirements for satisfactory performance in this position. It is not to be construed as an exhaustive statement of the duties, responsibilities, or requirements of the position.
<br><br>
Applicants should send resumes tailored for this position to the following by August 1st:<br>
